description:
Dicot; opposite leaves; 
Key B;
Leaves present at anthesis; simple leaves; plants rooted in soil; not parasitic; perianth differentiated into sepals and petals; pistil 1; inferior ovary; bisexual; petals present; petals seperate; stamens 4; 
Cornaceae; 
Opposite leaves; flowers greenish; in a close cyme substended by 4 showy white bracts;
Cornus florida

4 4 4 / 1^2

Dicot woody genera with plants erect and >2 dm tall, leaves simple, opposite; 
leaf margin not toothed, the blade unlobed, leaves <1.5 dm long, crushed leaves not aromatic, leaf blades not glandular-dotted, lateral veins arching upwards, becoming parallel or nearly so with the midrib; 
Leaves opposite; Flowers greenish in a head and subtended by 4 showy, white, bracts; 
Flower formula: * 4 4 4 /1^2
